<title>ECUADOR: Paraguay joins Andean Development Corp.</title>
<headline>Paraguay joins Andean Development Corp.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Paraguay joined the Andean Development Corp (CAF) Tuesday, bringing the total number of member countries to 10, a CAF statement said.</p>
<p>It said Paraguay bought 1,000 shares in the corporation, valued at $9.7 million.</p>
<p>The CAF is the financial arm of the Andean group of countries and finances public and private sector infrastructure projects in the member countries.</p>
<p>The Andean group is made up of Bolivia, Colombia, Ecuador, Peru and Venezuela but the CAF membership includes Brazil, Chile, Mexico and Trinidad and Tobago who are not Andean members.</p>
<p>In 1996, the ADC had a portfolio of loans and investments worth $2.73 billion.</p>
<p>((--Franz Bastidas, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258429))</p>
